repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/vulonviing/cross-constituency-aggregation-community-notes
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline and manuscript for Cross-Constituency Aggregation
  (CCA), an aggregation rule for X's Community Notes that requires a note to
  earn approval from every behavioral constituency rather than from a
  majority. The repository contains the 100k-note, 200k-rater spectral
  clustering pipeline, the scoring and topic-modeling stages, the two-stage
  Gemma 4 31B validation of the rescue set, and every committed artifact needed
  to re-derive the paper's results.
keywords:
  - community notes
  - crowdsourced fact-checking
  - social choice
  - spectral clustering
  - content moderation
  - bridging algorithms
license: MIT
